    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).\n\n## What I changed\n\n**Version-2 identity derivation** \u2014 every identifier now mixes in a fixed `V2` tag, so no version-1 value can recur:\n- `util/Locality.java` \u2014 added the `IDENTITY_VERSION_TAG = \"V2\"` constant and `identityRegion(city, postcode)`, which returns the plain region prefixed with `V2` (e.g. `V2NSW`). The plain `of(...)` is untouched, so `locality`/`timezone` stay plain.\n- `AssignMemberId.java` \u2014 the `memberId`'s region segment now comes from `Locality.identityRegion(...)` \u2192 e.g. `V2NSW2716E6609E7` (was `NSW2716E6609E1`).\n- `OwnerIdentity.java` \u2014 `key(...)` and `householdId(...)` now fold the `V2` tag into their SHA-256 preimage. Because the tag is a global constant, every value changes while duplicate-detection and household-grouping comparisons are unaffected.\n\n**Response shape (`apiVersion` + nested `identity`)**:\n- `resources/openapi.yml` \u2014 removed top-level `memberId`/`householdId`/`identityKey` from `Owner`, added a top-level integer `apiVersion` and an `identity` object referencing a new `Identity` schema holding the three identifiers.\n- `mapper/OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 maps `apiVersion` = 2 and builds the nested `IdentityDto` (member id and household id from the entity, identity key derived).\n\n**Audit event \u2192 schema version 2**:\n- `OwnerCreatedEvent.java` \u2014 JSON now emits `\"schemaVersion\":2` and an `ownerSegment`.\n- `AuditOwnerCreated.java` \u2014 recomputes the owner segment from the version-2 identity (with the plain region, so the `V2` tag never reaches the segment).\n\nRequest fields are unchanged. The `locality` (`NSW`), `timezone`, and the owner-segment's derived region all remain plain \u2014 the `V2` tag appears only inside the identifiers, confirmed in the audit output: `memberId=V2NSW2716E6609E7`, `ownerSegment:\"STANDARD_METRO\"`.",
