    "probe_text": "I now have the complete pipeline. Here is what happens, in order, for `POST /api/owners`.\n\n## Gate (before any step)\n\n- **Authorization** \u2014 `hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')`; otherwise `AuthorizationDeniedException` (403).\n\n## Pipeline (in execution order)\n\n**1. `CheckIdempotencyKey`** \u2014 *branch, no mutation.* Reads the `Idempotency-Key` header (blank = absent). If that key was already recorded from a prior successful create, branches to **replay**: `RespondWithReplayedOwner` loads that original owner and returns **200** (or `NotFoundException`/404 if it's since gone) \u2014 the rest of the pipeline is skipped. No key, or an unseen key, proceeds to create.\n\n**2. `ValidateRequiredOwnerFields`** \u2014 *validation + mutation.* Binds the body (no `@Valid`). Normalizes the address (trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand abbreviations) \u2014 structured `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` preferred, flat `address` accepted for compatibility. Rejects with `MissingRequiredFieldsException` (**400**) if any of **firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone** is missing/blank *after* normalization. Side-effect: writes back the normalized address lines and composed `address`, and republishes the body as a variable for later steps.\n\n**3. `ValidateOwnerPostcode`** \u2014 *validation only.* Only if a postcode is present: must be exactly 4 digits, and if the city's region is known (Sydney\u2192NSW 2000\u20132099, Melbourne\u2192VIC 3000\u20133099, Brisbane\u2192QLD 4000\u20134099) must fall in range. Unknown city accepts any 4-digit code. Else `InvalidPostcodeException` (**400**).\n\n**4. `ValidateOwnerRegistrationDate`** \u2014 *validation only.* Only if `registrationDate` is present: must not be after the server date. Else `FutureRegistrationDateException` (**400**).\n\n**5. `NormalizeOwnerTelephone`** \u2014 *validation + mutation.* Rewrites telephone to E.164 (strip spaces/dashes/brackets; keep leading `+cc` or assume `+61` and drop one leading `0`; must yield 8\u201315 digits). Writes it back. Invalid \u2192 `InvalidTelephoneException` (**400**).\n\n**6. `NormalizeOwnerEmail`** \u2014 *validation + mutation.* Only if email present/non-blank: trim + lower-case, must be syntactically valid and its domain not on the disposable-domain blocklist; writes normalized value back. Else `InvalidEmailException` (**400**).\n\n**7. `EnsureUniqueOwnerIdentity`** *(transaction begins)* \u2014 *validation only.* Unless `sharesHousehold: true` (which bypasses this entirely), computes `identityKey` = SHA-256 over (E.164 telephone, lower-cased email, soundex(lastName)) and scans all non-deleted owners; an exact whole-key match is a hard duplicate \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` (**409**).\n\n**8. `EnsureCityBelowCapacity`** \u2014 *validation only.* Counts owners in the same city (case-insensitive, whitespace-collapsed); if \u2265 **50** \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` (**409**).\n\n**9. `EnsureBelowDailyLimit`** \u2014 *validation only.* Rolls the effective registration date (supplied or server date) forward onto a business day; counts existing owners with that `registrationDate`; if \u2265 **100** \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitException` (**429**).\n\n**10. `BuildOwner`** \u2014 *side-effect (construct).* Maps DTO \u2192 `Owner`; defaults registration date to today if absent; snaps registration date to a business day. Publishes the `Owner`.\n\n**11. `AssignOwnerHousehold`** \u2014 *side-effect.* Sets deterministic `householdId` = f(lastName, postcode).\n\n**12. `AssignMemberId`** \u2014 *side-effect.* Computes `memberId` `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>` (V2 identity region from postcode/city, fiscal year, SHA-256 hash, Luhn check digit); appends `-2`, `-3`, \u2026 on collision with an existing `memberId`.\n\n**13. `CountNamesakes`** \u2014 *side-effect.* Sets `namesakeCount` = existing owners sharing first+last name (case-insensitive).\n\n**14. `CountHouseholdMembers`** \u2014 *side-effect.* Sets `householdSize` = existing same-household owners + 1 (this new one).\n\n**15. `CapMembershipLevel`** \u2014 *side-effect.* Derives the membership level and caps it at (max level among existing household members) + 1; sets `membershipLevel`.\n\n**16. `FlagPossibleDuplicate`** \u2014 *side-effect.* Unless `sharesHousehold` (then flags cleared): if a non-deleted owner has a *different* identityKey but matching soundex(lastName) **and** postcode, sets `possibleDuplicate=true` and `possibleDuplicateOf` = lowest matching id; otherwise clears them.\n\n**17. `SaveOwner`** \u2014 *side-effect (persist).* `ownerRepository.save(owner)` \u2014 owner id populated here.\n\n**18. `AuditOwnerCreated`** \u2014 *side-effect (logging).* Emits a human-readable line and a JSON `OwnerCreatedEvent` (schema v2, monotonic `seq`, memberId, recomputed segment) on the `AUDIT` logger.\n\n**19. `EnqueueWelcomeNotification`** \u2014 *side-effect (logging).* Emits a `NOTIFY` line with owner id + memberId.\n\n**20. `EvaluateBulkSignupWarning`** \u2014 *side-effect.* Sets transient `bulkSignupWarning=true` if > **80** owners share the business-day registration date (counted after save).\n\n**21. `EvaluateCapacityWarning`** \u2014 *side-effect.* Sets transient `capacityWarning=true` if the city already holds **40\u201349** other owners (excluding this one).\n\n**22. `RecordIdempotencyKey`** \u2014 *side-effect.* If the request carried an `Idempotency-Key`, records key \u2192 new owner id (in-memory) so future repeats replay.\n\n**23. `RespondWithOwnerCreated`** *(transaction commits at pipeline end)* \u2014 *side-effect (respond).* Maps owner \u2192 DTO and returns **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Steps 7\u201323 all run under `govern: [ transaction ]`, so persistence and idempotency-key recording commit once at the end; any escalation there rolls the create back. (The in-memory idempotency and audit/notify log lines are not transactional in the DB sense.)\n- Validation ordering is deliberate: required-fields \u2192 postcode \u2192 registration date \u2192 phone \u2192 email \u2192 uniqueness \u2192 city capacity \u2192 daily limit \u2014 so a bad body yields the specific 400 before the 409/429 capacity checks.\n- Unmatched escalations fall through to the generic handlers (`DataIntegrityViolationException`, `Exception`, `MethodArgumentNotValidException`).\n\nI didn't change anything."
